avmosaic — third-party components
===================================

This repository contains only avmosaic's own source code (MIT, see LICENSE),
one public-domain test image, and a demo image derived from it. The components
below are installed separately as Python packages or downloaded at runtime; they
are not vendored here and keep their own licenses.

NudeNet (detector models: 320n.onnx, 640m.onnx)
  https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet
  IMPORTANT: the PyPI package "nudenet" 3.4.x declares the MIT license, but the
  GitHub repository (which also hosts the 640m weights) is licensed AGPL-3.0.
  If you redistribute avmosaic together with NudeNet or its weights, or offer
  it as a network service, check which license applies to you. A detector of
  your own can be plugged in through the Python API instead.

ONNX Runtime — MIT — https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
OpenCV (opencv-python-headless) — Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python
NumPy — BSD-3-Clause — https://numpy.org
imageio-ffmpeg — BSD-2-Clause — https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg
  Its wheels include an ffmpeg binary, which is a separate program under the
  (L)GPL and is run as a subprocess.

tests/data/david_statue.mp4 (generated by tests/data/make_statue_clip.py)
  From "Replica Michelangelo's David black background.jpg" by Jebulon, Wikimedia
  Commons, CC0 1.0.

tests/data/astronaut.jpg, docs/demo.jpg
  Portrait of astronaut Eileen Collins, NASA, public domain (the same image as
  scikit-image's data.astronaut()).
